# Client-side routing.
#
# Deep links must serve index.html so a refresh on /group/awards loads the
# router instead of 404ing. Verified against `wrangler pages dev`: /, /me/admin,
# /group/awards and /chat/thread all return index.html with a 200.
#
# Wrangler warns that this rule "loops" and reports ignoring it — Pages' own
# SPA fallback covers the same cases either way. The rule stays because the
# fallback is implicit platform behaviour and this is the documented, explicit
# way to ask for it; the warning is cosmetic and the outcome is identical.
#
# /api/* is deliberately NOT covered. Functions take precedence over both
# static assets and this file, so /api/food-scan reaches the Function — a
# catch-all here would otherwise hand the scanner HTML where it expects JSON.
/*    /index.html   200
